# Tailwind CSS Standards

**WORKSPACE RULE - ALWAYS APPLY**

## Purpose
Maintain consistent styling approach using Tailwind utility classes

## Guidelines
- Use Tailwind utility classes exclusively for styling
- No custom CSS files except globals.css for base styles
- Prefer utility classes over inline styles
- Use responsive prefixes (sm:, md:, lg:) for breakpoints
- Leverage Tailwind's color palette and spacing scale
- Use semantic class combinations for common patterns

## Common Patterns
```tsx
// Cards
className="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-lg p-6"

// Buttons
className="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded-md hover:bg-blue-700"

// Forms
className="w-full px-3 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-md focus:ring-blue-500"

// Layout
className="max-w-7xl mx-auto p-6"
```

## Avoid
- Custom CSS modules
- Inline styles
- Non-Tailwind class names